      "end": 1.45,
      "text": "Hey, how are you doing?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 10.65,
      "end": 17.72,
      "text": "Thirty people means a blink in almost every frame, so the trick is taking lots. Use burst mode, or take at least ten in a row."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 22.47,
      "end": 28.66,
      "text": "Tell them it's quick and keep talking while you shoot. Counting down to three and shooting on two catches people before they blink."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 31.56,
      "end": 38.81,
      "text": "Also arrange them in rows on steps if there are any. Tall people at the back, kids at the front, and make sure you can see every face."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 44.07,
      "end": 50.151,
      "text": "Use a timer and a tripod, or hand the camera to a neighbour for the last few. You belong in the family photo too."
    }
